  "live_records": {
    "q-35247": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35247",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}-4(5)=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+5=9.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
